You are working on an OpenNMS AI Monitoring MCP (Minimum Credible Product).

This system integrates with an existing OpenNMS infrastructure using XML-based REST APIs and builds an AI-assisted NOC operations platform.

────────────────────────────────────────
🎯 CORE OBJECTIVE
────────────────────────────────────────
Build a production-aligned MCP that:
- Ingests OpenNMS alarms, nodes, events, outages
- Stores all data in PostgreSQL (raw + normalized)
- Generates AI-based troubleshooting suggestions for CRITICAL alerts
- Collects operator feedback for continuous improvement
- Provides a chat interface for incident follow-ups
- Supports LDAP authentication and role-based access

Primary KPI:
→ Reduce MTTR (Mean Time To Resolution)

────────────────────────────────────────
⚙️ TECH STACK (MANDATORY)
────────────────────────────────────────
Backend:
- Python 3.12+
- FastAPI
- SQLAlchemy (ORM)
- Alembic (migrations)
- PostgreSQL
- lxml / xml.etree for XML parsing
- ldap3 (LDAP authentication)
- requests (OpenNMS API calls)

Frontend:
- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript ONLY
- No frameworks (React/Vue/Angular prohibited)

LLM Layer:
- Primary: Ollama (local LLM)
- Optional: OpenAI / Anthropic / OpenRouter
- Must support provider abstraction layer

Infrastructure:
- Bare metal Linux
- Internal deployment only
- No Kubernetes in MCP phase

────────────────────────────────────────
🧠 ARCHITECTURE RULES
────────────────────────────────────────
1. Always design BEFORE coding
2. Never assume OpenNMS returns JSON (it is XML)
3. Always store:
   - raw OpenNMS payload
   - parsed normalized data

4. Use service-layer architecture:
   - API Layer (FastAPI routes)
   - Service Layer (business logic)
   - Repository Layer (DB access)
   - Connector Layer (OpenNMS integration)

5. Keep components loosely coupled

6. MCP is NOT a toy system:
   - design must support 2000+ servers

────────────────────────────────────────
📊 DATA RULES
────────────────────────────────────────
- Never discard OpenNMS fields
- Always store raw XML in DB (or JSONB equivalent after conversion)
- Use UPSERT for alerts and nodes (no duplicates allowed)
- Maintain full alert lifecycle tracking:
  - ACTIVE
  - ACKNOWLEDGED
  - RESOLVED
  - CLEARED

Node naming convention:
{operator}-{circle}-{ip}-{server_type}

Parse and store separately:
- operator
- circle
- ip_address
- server_type

────────────────────────────────────────
🤖 AI SYSTEM RULES
────────────────────────────────────────
AI is strictly ADVISORY ONLY.

AI MUST:
- Provide troubleshooting steps
- Suggest possible causes
- Summarize incident context
- Provide confidence score (if possible)

AI MUST NOT:
- Execute commands
- Modify infrastructure
- Restart services
- Take autonomous actions

AI Processing Flow:
1. Context Builder
2. Event/Alert Summarizer
3. Diagnostic Reasoning
4. Recommendation Generator

────────────────────────────────────────
🔐 SECURITY RULES
────────────────────────────────────────
- LDAP authentication is mandatory
- Role-based access control required:

Roles:
- noc-viewer (read-only)
- noc-operator (acknowledge + feedback + chat)
- noc-admin (full access)

Data sanitization BEFORE LLM calls:
- Remove IP addresses → [IP]
- Remove emails → [EMAIL]
- Remove secrets/tokens → [REDACTED]
- Truncate large logs (max token budget enforced)

Never send raw sensitive infrastructure data to LLM.

────────────────────────────────────────
🧾 DATABASE RULES
────────────────────────────────────────
PostgreSQL is the system of record.

Must include tables for:
- nodes
- alerts
- alert_history
- feedback
- chat_messages
- llm_responses
- audit_logs

Rules:
- Always use migrations (Alembic)
- Always define indexes for query performance
- Always support auditability

────────────────────────────────────────
🌐 OPENNMS INTEGRATION RULES
────────────────────────────────────────
- Use OpenNMS REST APIs (XML-based responses)
- Use Basic Auth or configured auth method
- Build dedicated connector layer:
  - XML fetcher
  - XML parser
  - normalization engine

Ingestion must:
- handle retries
- avoid duplicates
- log every sync cycle
- support incremental updates

────────────────────────────────────────
🧑‍💻 FRONTEND RULES
────────────────────────────────────────
- Must be extremely simple and fast
- Must prioritize NOC usability over design aesthetics
- Must minimize clicks during incidents

Pages:
- Login (LDAP)
- Dashboard (critical alerts)
- Alert details
- Chat
- Feedback panel

UI rules:
- Show only essential fields by default
- Hide advanced metadata behind expandable sections

────────────────────────────────────────
📡 LOGGING & AUDIT RULES
────────────────────────────────────────
Log every important action:
- user login
- alert view
- AI recommendation generation
- feedback submission
- chat interactions

Logs must be immutable and queryable.

────────────────────────────────────────
⚡ PERFORMANCE RULES
────────────────────────────────────────
- Design for high-frequency ingestion (multiple servers)
- Avoid blocking API calls
- Use background tasks for ingestion if needed
- Ensure DB queries are optimized

────────────────────────────────────────
📦 IMPLEMENTATION DISCIPLINE
────────────────────────────────────────
When implementing:

1. Understand requirement fully
2. Identify dependencies
3. Design data flow
4. Implement backend first
5. Then DB
6. Then AI layer
7. Then frontend

NEVER jump directly into UI without backend logic.

────────────────────────────────────────
🚫 ANTI-PATTERNS (STRICTLY FORBIDDEN)
────────────────────────────────────────
- No mock APIs in final code
- No hardcoded secrets
- No skipping sanitization
- No direct LLM calls from controllers
- No duplicate alert records
- No business logic in frontend

────────────────────────────────────────
🎯 FINAL GOAL
────────────────────────────────────────
Build a clean MCP that:

- Works reliably with OpenNMS
- Assists NOC engineers during incidents
- Reduces MTTR using AI guidance
- Collects structured feedback
- Is simple enough for real operator usage
